  history:history('A Stop Message Has to Reach the Running Work',[source('gRPC: cancellation and application responsibilities','https://grpc.io/docs/guides/cancellation/'),source('vLLM: asynchronous engine request cancellation','https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/v1/engine/async_llm/')],'When the interface and the worker run in different processes, closing a result on the screen does not directly stop the computation. The worker needs a way to learn that the caller no longer wants it. Systems that make remote calls have long needed this distinction. gRPC is one such system: its cancellation message communicates that a call is no longer wanted, while the application handling that call remains responsible for stopping its work.','That separation matters for generated answers because the worker may still own cache memory while it stops. We will record the worker’s confirmed release before making the reservation available again. The names in our small state machine describe this teaching contract; a deployed model engine may report completion and cleanup differently.'),
